# SOC Home Lab — Network Discovery & Wireshark Baseline

[![Nmap](https://img.shields.io/badge/Nmap-7.99-purple)]()
[![Wireshark](https://img.shields.io/badge/Wireshark-Baseline-1679A7?logo=wireshark&logoColor=white)]()
[![MITRE](https://img.shields.io/badge/MITRE%20ATT%26CK-3%20Techniques-CC0000)](https://attack.mitre.org/)

> Documented internal network discovery and traffic baseline assessment of an authorized residential SOC lab. Two professional forensic reports with SHA-256 chain of custody. Five findings identified including SMB exposure on perimeter router and Intel AMT presence on workstation.

---

## What's Inside

| Report | What It Covers | Findings |
|--------|----------------|----------|
| **Network Discovery & Risk Assessment** | Nmap scan of `192.168.2.0/24`, 3 live hosts identified | 5 (1 High, 1 Medium, 2 Low, 1 Info) |
| **Network Traffic Baseline Analysis** | 5.5-min Wireshark capture, 4,665 packets, 28 TLS destinations | 4 + 1 baseline observation |

---

## Key Findings

| ID | Finding | MITRE | Risk |
|----|---------|-------|------|
| F-001 | SMB exposed on perimeter router | T1021.002 | 🟠 High |
| F-002 | Intel AMT (CVE-2017-5689) detected | — | 🟡 Medium |
| F-006 | WPAD name resolution requests | T1557.001 | 🟡 Medium |
| F-007 | Unknown LAN host found via passive monitoring | T1046 | 🟢 Low |
| F-008 | Plaintext DNS resolution | T1040 | 🟢 Low |

